IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`
IMPORT `wra1-three-valued`

-- wra1-ch2-responsibilities.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), Part 1, Chapter 2 (sections 13 to 29), part wra1.
-- LAYER 1, the law objectively: it takes nobody's point of view.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Reading an answer (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer):
--   FALSE / JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (quoted in a FALSE-kind comment), or a supplied regulation says no
--   NOTHING            = not covered (the reason is in a NOTHING-kind comment)
-- Judgments the Act hands to the Secretary of State ("in the opinion of the Secretary of State") and meanings it leaves to
-- regulations ("prescribed", "such meaning as may be prescribed") are plain inputs, never guessed.
-- The groups of claimants are applied in the order the text itself uses (s 21(1) "does not fall within section 19 or 20",
-- s 22(1) "not falling within any of sections 19 to 21"): see fork F-groups in NOTES.md.

§ `Section 13 -- Work-related requirements: introductory`

-- (1) "claimants must comply" is the duty of the claimant; the Secretary of State imposes the requirement. The duty has no
-- time limit of its own: the time comes from the requirement imposed (ss 15 to 18, 23), which the Act does not fix.
DECLARE `s 13(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 13(1) the claimant`
    `s 13(1) the Secretary of State`

DECLARE `s 13(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 13(1) complies with the work-related requirement imposed`
    `s 22(2)(a) imposes a work search requirement`
    `s 22(2)(b) imposes a work availability requirement`
    `s 19(1) imposes a work-related requirement`
    `s 24(5)(b) imposes another requirement`

-- src:130 | (1) This Chapter provides for the Secretary of State to impose work-related requirements with which claimants must comply for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 13(1) (src:130-130)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 13(1) party` `s 13(1) action`
`s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement imposed` MEANS
    PARTY `s 13(1) the claimant`
    MUST `s 13(1) complies with the work-related requirement imposed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 13(1) the claimant` BECAUSE "the claimant did not comply with a work-related requirement imposed under this Chapter (ss 26 and 27 say when the award is then reduced)"

-- The same duty as a decision function (the stable binary prints a #TRACE outcome but cannot assert it).
@ref s 13(1) (src:130-130)
GIVEN `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement` MEANS
    IF `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the claimant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to comply with "work-related requirements" the Secretary of State imposes; where none is imposed the section is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2) the four work-related requirements and the section that defines each.
-- src:131 | (2) In this Part “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:132 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 15);
-- src:133 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 16);
-- src:134 | (c) a work search requirement (see section 17);
-- src:135 | (d) a work availability requirement (see section 18).
@ref s 13(2) (src:131-135)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Work-related requirement`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 13(2) the section that defines the work-related requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `work-focused interview requirement` THEN "section 15"
    WHEN `work preparation requirement` THEN "section 16"
    WHEN `work search requirement` THEN "section 17"
    WHEN `work availability requirement` THEN "section 18"

-- (3) the four groups and the section that describes each.
-- src:136 | (3) The work-related requirements which may be imposed on a claimant depend on which of the following groups the claimant falls into—
-- src:137 | (a) no work-related requirements (see section 19);
-- src:138 | (b) work-focused interview requirement only (see section 20);
-- src:139 | (c) work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only (see section 21);
-- src:140 | (d) all work-related requirements (see section 22).
@ref s 13(3) (src:136-140)
GIVEN group IS A `Group of claimants by requirement`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 13(3) the section that describes the group` MEANS
    CONSIDER group
    WHEN `no work-related requirements` THEN "section 19"
    WHEN `work-focused interview requirement only` THEN "section 20"
    WHEN `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only` THEN "section 21"
    WHEN `all work-related requirements` THEN "section 22"

§ `Section 14 -- Claimant commitment`

-- (1) "A claimant commitment is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of universal credit."
-- src:142 | (1) A claimant commitment is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of universal credit.
@ref s 14(1) (src:142-142)
GIVEN `it is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the document is a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is a record of a claimant's responsibilities ..." (a definition)
    `it is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of universal credit`

-- (2) "is to be prepared by the Secretary of State and may be reviewed and updated as the Secretary of State thinks fit";
-- s 29(1) lets an authorised person exercise the Secretary of State's functions under ss 13 to 25.
-- src:143 | (2) A claimant commitment is to be prepared by the Secretary of State and may be reviewed and updated as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 14(2) (src:143-143)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2) this authority prepares, reviews and updates the claimant commitment` MEANS
    CONSIDER authority
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- composition with s 29(1), not the words of s 14(2): the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25 may be exercised by an authorised person (listed under "Marginal readings for a lawyer" in NOTES.md)
    WHEN `an authorised person` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names the Secretary of State only; no other authority is mentioned
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (3) "to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit": the judgment is the Secretary of State's, so it is an input.
-- src:144 | (3) A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 14(3) (src:144-144)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit"; a form the Secretary of State does not think fit is outside the grant
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) "is to include (a) a record of the requirements ..., (b) any prescribed information, and (c) any other information the
-- Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include."
DECLARE `s 14(4) item in a claimant commitment` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(4)(a) a record of the requirements the claimant must comply with`
    `s 14(4)(b) any prescribed information`
    `s 14(4)(c) any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
    `s 14(4) some other item`

-- src:145 | (4) A claimant commitment is to include—
-- src:146 | (a) a record of the requirements that the claimant must comply with under this Part (or such of them as the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include),
-- src:147 | (b) any prescribed information, and
-- src:148 | (c) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include.
@ref s 14(4) (src:145-148)
GIVEN item IS A `s 14(4) item in a claimant commitment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(4) the claimant commitment is to include` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 14(4)(a) a record of the requirements the claimant must comply with` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 14(4)(b) any prescribed information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 14(4)(c) any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is to include" does not say that nothing else may be included
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (5) "a claimant accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such
-- manner as may be prescribed". The manner is for regulations (and s 4(7)), so it is an input.
-- src:149 | (5) For the purposes of this Part a claimant accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 14(5) (src:149-149)
GIVEN `the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepts it in the manner regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` MEANS
    IF `the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the claimant accepts it in the manner regulations prescribe`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed"
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner is prescribed; regulations are not among the sources
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 15 -- Work-focused interview requirement`

-- (1) "a requirement that a claimant participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State"
-- src:152 | (1) In this Part a “work-focused interview requirement” is a requirement that a claimant participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 15(1) (src:152-152)
GIVEN `it requires the claimant to participate in one or more work-focused interviews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interviews are as specified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the requirement is a work-focused interview requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'work-focused interview requirement' is a requirement that a claimant participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State" (a definition)
    `it requires the claimant to participate in one or more work-focused interviews`
    AND `the interviews are as specified by the Secretary of State`

-- (2) "an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation"
-- src:153 | (2) A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation.
@ref s 15(2) (src:153-153)
GIVEN `the interview is for purposes relating to work or work preparation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes are among those regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the interview is a work-focused interview` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation" (a definition); NOTHING where the prescribed purposes are not supplied
    `s 3(1) both of these are true` (JUST `the interview is for purposes relating to work or work preparation`) `the purposes are among those regulations prescribe`

-- (3) "The purposes which may be prescribed ... include in particular that of making it more likely in the opinion of the
-- Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)."
-- src:154 | (3) The purposes which may be prescribed under subsection (2) include in particular that of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 15(3) (src:154-154)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the purpose makes it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work, more paid work or better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3) the purpose may be prescribed under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the purpose makes it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work, more paid work or better-paid work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include in particular" does not close the list of purposes
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) "The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where a work-focused interview is to take place."
DECLARE `s 15(4) matter about an interview` IS ONE OF
    `s 15(4) how the interview is to take place`
    `s 15(4) when the interview is to take place`
    `s 15(4) where the interview is to take place`
    `s 15(4) some other matter`

-- src:155 | (4) The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where a work-focused interview is to take place.
@ref s 15(4) (src:155-155)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 15(4) matter about an interview`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(4) the Secretary of State may specify this for a work-focused interview` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 15(4) how the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(4) when the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(4) where the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "how, when and where" are the matters the grant names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 16 -- Work preparation requirement`

-- (1) "a requirement that a claimant take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it
-- more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or
-- better-paid work)"
-- src:157 | (1) In this Part a “work preparation requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 16(1) (src:157-157)
GIVEN `it requires the claimant to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the claimant will obtain paid work, more paid work or better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the requirement is a work preparation requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'work preparation requirement' is a requirement that a claimant take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose ..." (a definition)
    `it requires the claimant to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State`
    AND `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the claimant will obtain paid work, more paid work or better-paid work`

-- (2) "The Secretary of State may under subsection (1) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action."
-- src:158 | (2) The Secretary of State may under subsection (1) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action.
@ref s 16(2) (src:158-158)
GIVEN `an action has been specified under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) the Secretary of State may specify the time to be devoted to the action` MEANS
    IF `an action has been specified under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to any particular action" specified under subsection (1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) "Action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes in particular (a) ... (g) any action prescribed for the purpose"
DECLARE `s 16(3) kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `s 16(3)(a) attending a skills assessment`
    `s 16(3)(b) improving personal presentation`
    `s 16(3)(c) participating in training`
    `s 16(3)(d) participating in an employment programme`
    `s 16(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement`
    `s 16(3)(f) developing a business plan`
    `s 16(3)(g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)`
    `s 16(3) some other action`

-- src:159 | (3) Action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes in particular—
-- src:160 | (a) attending a skills assessment;
-- src:161 | (b) improving personal presentation;
-- src:162 | (c) participating in training;
-- src:163 | (d) participating in an employment programme;
-- src:164 | (e) undertaking work experience or a work placement;
-- src:165 | (f) developing a business plan;
-- src:166 | (g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1).
@ref s 16(3) (src:159-166)
GIVEN action IS A `s 16(3) kind of action`
      `regulations prescribe the action for the purpose in subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the action may be specified under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER action
    WHEN `s 16(3)(a) attending a skills assessment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(3)(b) improving personal presentation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(3)(c) participating in training` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(3)(d) participating in an employment programme` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(3)(f) developing a business plan` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (g) is any action regulations prescribe; where supplied the answer is the regulations' own
    WHEN `s 16(3)(g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)` THEN `regulations prescribe the action for the purpose in subsection (1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes in particular" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (4) "In the case of a person with limited capability for work, the action which may be specified under subsection (1)
-- includes taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment." The determination of limited capability is an input (s 37(3)).
-- src:167 | (4) In the case of a person with limited capability for work, the action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment.
@ref s 16(4) (src:167-167)
GIVEN `the person has limited capability for work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(4) the action may include taking part in a work-focused health-related assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person has limited capability for work`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a person with limited capability for work"; a person outside that description is not covered
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): limited capability for work is determined in accordance with regulations (s 37(3))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (5) "'work-focused health-related assessment' means an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary
-- of State which is carried out for the purpose of assessing (a) ... and (b) such other matters ... as may be prescribed."
-- src:168 | (5) In subsection (4) “work-focused health-related assessment” means an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State which is carried out for the purpose of assessing—
-- src:169 | (a) the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition, and
-- src:170 | (b) such other matters relating to their physical or mental condition and the likelihood of their obtaining or remaining in work or being able to do so as may be prescribed.
@ref s 16(5) (src:168-170)
GIVEN `it is an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it assesses the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it also assesses the other matters regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(5) the assessment is a work-focused health-related assessment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'work-focused health-related assessment' means an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State which is carried out for the purpose of assessing (a) ... and (b) ..."
    `s 3(1) both of these are true`
        (`s 3(1) both of these are true`
            (JUST `it is an assessment by a health care professional approved by the Secretary of State`)
            (JUST `it assesses the extent to which the person's capability for work may be improved by taking steps in relation to their physical or mental condition`))
        `it also assesses the other matters regulations prescribe`

-- (6) "'health care professional' means (a) a registered medical practitioner, (b) a registered nurse, (c) an occupational
-- therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the
-- Health Act 1999, or (d) a member of such other profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National
-- Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002 as may be prescribed."
DECLARE `s 16(6) kind of professional` IS ONE OF
    `s 16(6)(a) a registered medical practitioner`
    `s 16(6)(b) a registered nurse`
    `s 16(6)(c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist`
    `s 16(6)(d) a member of another profession`
    `s 16(6) someone else`

-- src:171 | (6) In subsection (5) “health care professional” means—
-- src:172 | (a) a registered medical practitioner,
-- src:173 | (b) a registered nurse,
-- src:174 | (c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999, or
-- src:175 | (d) a member of such other profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002 as may be prescribed.
@ref s 16(6) (src:171-175)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 16(6) kind of professional`
      `registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profession is one regulations prescribe, regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the 2002 Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(6) the person is a health care professional` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 16(6)(a) a registered medical practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 16(6)(b) a registered nurse` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999"
    WHEN `s 16(6)(c) an occupational therapist or physiotherapist` THEN JUST `registered with a regulatory body established by an Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (d) is a profession regulations prescribe; where supplied the answer is the regulations' own
    WHEN `s 16(6)(d) a member of another profession` THEN `the profession is one regulations prescribe, regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the 2002 Act`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'health care professional' means" (a)-(d)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 17 -- Work search requirement`

-- (1) "a requirement that a claimant take (a) all reasonable action, and (b) any particular action specified by the Secretary
-- of State, for the purpose of obtaining paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)"
-- src:177 | (1) In this Part a “work search requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take—
-- src:178 | (a) all reasonable action, and
-- src:179 | (b) any particular action specified by the Secretary of State,
-- src:180 | for the purpose of obtaining paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 17(1) (src:177-180)
GIVEN `it requires the claimant to take all reasonable action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the claimant to take any particular action specified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is obtaining paid work, more paid work or better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the requirement is a work search requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'work search requirement' is a requirement that a claimant take (a) all reasonable action, and (b) any particular action specified by the Secretary of State, for the purpose of obtaining paid work ..." (a definition)
    `it requires the claimant to take all reasonable action`
    AND `it requires the claimant to take any particular action specified by the Secretary of State`
    AND `the purpose is obtaining paid work, more paid work or better-paid work`

-- (2) "The Secretary of State may under subsection (1)(b) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action."
-- src:181 | (2) The Secretary of State may under subsection (1)(b) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action.
