      `the claimant is willing immediately to take up paid work, more paid work or better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant meets the definition regulations give of being able and willing immediately` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the claimant is available for work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claimant meets the definition regulations give of being able and willing immediately`
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'available for work' means able and willing immediately to take up paid work"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `the claimant is able immediately to take up paid work, more paid work or better-paid work`
        AND `the claimant is willing immediately to take up paid work, more paid work or better-paid work`

-- (3) "Regulations may impose limitations on a work availability requirement ...; and the Secretary of State may in any
-- particular case specify further such limitations."
DECLARE `s 18(3) who may impose a limitation` IS ONE OF
