§ `Section 19 -- Claimants subject to no work-related requirements`

-- (6) "'responsible carer', in relation to a child, means (a) a single person who is responsible for the child, or (b) a
-- person who is a member of a couple where (i) the person or the other member of the couple is responsible for the child,
-- and (ii) the person has been nominated by the couple jointly as responsible for the child." Whether someone is
-- "responsible" for a child is for regulations (Schedule 1 paragraph 5(1)); the nomination is for regulations too (para 5(2)).
-- src:223 | (6) In this Part “responsible carer”, in relation to a child means—
-- src:224 | (a) a single person who is responsible for the child, or
-- src:225 | (b) a person who is a member of a couple where—
