      `the other member of the couple is responsible for the child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the couple has jointly nominated the person as responsible for the child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) the person is the responsible carer for the child` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of a couple`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'responsible carer' ... means ... (b) a person who is a member of a couple where (i) ... and (ii) the person has been nominated by the couple jointly"
    THEN `s 3(1) both of these are true`
            (`s 19(2) either of these is true` `the person is responsible for the child` `the other member of the couple is responsible for the child`)
            `the couple has jointly nominated the person as responsible for the child`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'responsible carer' ... means (a) a single person who is responsible for the child"
    ELSE `the person is responsible for the child`

-- (2) "A claimant falls within this section if (a) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity,
-- (b) ... regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person, (c) ... the responsible carer for
-- a child under the age of 1, or (d) ... of a prescribed description." Limited capability, caring responsibilities and
-- "severely disabled" are determined or defined by regulations, so each limb is a MAYBE input.
