      `the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is the responsible carer for a child under the age of 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is of a description regulations prescribe under subsection (2)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the claimant falls within section 19` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant falls within this section if (a) ... (d)" (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a)), when every limb is known to fail
    `s 19(2) either of these is true`
        (`s 19(2) either of these is true` `the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity` `the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`)
        (`s 19(2) either of these is true` `the claimant is the responsible carer for a child under the age of 1` `the claimant is of a description regulations prescribe under subsection (2)(d)`)

-- (1) "The Secretary of State may not impose any work-related requirement on a claimant falling within this section."
