§ `Section 22 -- Claimants subject to all work-related requirements`

-- (1) "A claimant not falling within any of sections 19 to 21 falls within this section."
-- src:244 | (1) A claimant not falling within any of sections 19 to 21 falls within this section.
@ref s 22(1) (src:244-244)
GIVEN `the claimant falls within section 19` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within section 20` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within section 21` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the claimant falls within section 22` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant not falling within any of sections 19 to 21 falls within this section" (a claimant who does fall within one of them is not within this section)
    `s 4(1)(d) the opposite of this`
        (`s 19(2) either of these is true`
            (`s 19(2) either of these is true` `the claimant falls within section 19` `the claimant falls within section 20`)
            `the claimant falls within section 21`)

-- The group a claimant falls into (s 13(3)): section 19, then 20, then 21, then 22 (fork F-groups in NOTES.md).
-- src:136 | (3) The work-related requirements which may be imposed on a claimant depend on which of the following groups the claimant falls into—
-- src:137 | (a) no work-related requirements (see section 19);
-- src:138 | (b) work-focused interview requirement only (see section 20);
-- src:139 | (c) work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only (see section 21);
-- src:140 | (d) all work-related requirements (see section 22).
@ref s 13(3) (src:136-140)
GIVEN `the claimant falls within section 19` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within section 20` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within section 21` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Group of claimants by requirement`
`s 13(3) the group the claimant falls into` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claimant falls within section 19`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `no work-related requirements`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `the claimant falls within section 20`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `work-focused interview requirement only`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            CONSIDER `the claimant falls within section 21`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST `all work-related requirements`
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the claimant falls within section 21
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the claimant falls within section 20
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the claimant falls within section 19
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2) "The Secretary of State must, except in prescribed circumstances, impose on a claimant falling within this section (a)
-- a work search requirement, and (b) a work availability requirement." (3) "may ... impose either or both of ... (a) a
-- work-focused interview requirement; (b) a work preparation requirement."
-- src:245 | (2) The Secretary of State must, except in prescribed circumstances, impose on a claimant falling within this section—
-- src:246 | (a) a work search requirement, and
-- src:247 | (b) a work availability requirement.
@ref s 22(2) (src:245-247)
GIVEN `the claimant falls within section 22` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `prescribed circumstances apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      requirement IS A `Work-related requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the Secretary of State must impose this requirement on the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `work search requirement` THEN `the duty to impose`
    WHEN `work availability requirement` THEN `the duty to impose`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (3) gives only a power to impose a work-focused interview requirement or a work preparation requirement, not a duty
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the duty to impose` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claimant falls within section 22`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                CONSIDER `prescribed circumstances apply`
                -- FALSE-kind (a supplied regulation says no): "must, except in prescribed circumstances, impose": in prescribed circumstances there is no duty
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
                -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed circumstances are in regulations, not among the sources
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "a claimant falling within this section"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the claimant falls within section 22
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:248 | (3) The Secretary of State may, subject to this Part, impose either or both of the following on a claimant falling within this section—
-- src:249 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement;
-- src:250 | (b) a work preparation requirement.
@ref s 22(3) (src:248-250)
GIVEN `the claimant falls within section 22` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      requirement IS A `Work-related requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) the Secretary of State may impose this requirement on the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claimant falls within section 22`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER requirement
        WHEN `work-focused interview requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `work preparation requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the work search and work availability requirements are the subject of the duty in subsection (2), not of this power
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "a claimant falling within this section"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the claimant falls within section 22
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The duty in (2) as a regulative rule. "Except in prescribed circumstances" is a condition on the duty, not on the rule's
-- text, so the rule is run for a claimant to whom the duty applies. The text fixes no time for the duty.
-- src:245 | (2) The Secretary of State must, except in prescribed circumstances, impose on a claimant falling within this section—
-- src:246 | (a) a work search requirement, and
-- src:247 | (b) a work availability requirement.
@ref s 22(2) (src:245-247)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 13(1) party` `s 13(1) action`
`s 22(2) the Secretary of State must impose a work search requirement and a work availability requirement` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State`
     MUST `s 22(2)(a) imposes a work search requirement`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "no work search requirement was imposed on a claimant falling within section 22")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State`
     MUST `s 22(2)(b) imposes a work availability requirement`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "no work availability requirement was imposed on a claimant falling within section 22")

§ `Section 23 -- Connected requirements`

-- (1) "The Secretary of State may require a claimant to participate in an interview for any purpose relating to (a) the
-- imposition of a work-related requirement on the claimant; (b) verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related
-- requirement; (c) assisting the claimant to comply with a work-related requirement."
DECLARE `s 23(1) purpose of an interview` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(1)(a) the imposition of a work-related requirement on the claimant`
    `s 23(1)(b) verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement`
    `s 23(1)(c) assisting the claimant to comply with a work-related requirement`
    `s 23(1) some other purpose`

-- src:253 | (1) The Secretary of State may require a claimant to participate in an interview for any purpose relating to—
-- src:254 | (a) the imposition of a work-related requirement on the claimant;
-- src:255 | (b) verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement;
-- src:256 | (c) assisting the claimant to comply with a work-related requirement.
@ref s 23(1) (src:253-256)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 23(1) purpose of an interview`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the Secretary of State may require the claimant to participate in an interview for this purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 23(1)(a) the imposition of a work-related requirement on the claimant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 23(1)(b) verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 23(1)(c) assisting the claimant to comply with a work-related requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any purpose relating to" (a) to (c)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (2) "The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where such an interview is to take place."
DECLARE `s 23(2) matter about an interview` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(2) how the interview is to take place`
    `s 23(2) when the interview is to take place`
    `s 23(2) where the interview is to take place`
    `s 23(2) some other matter`

-- src:257 | (2) The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where such an interview is to take place.
@ref s 23(2) (src:257-257)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 23(2) matter about an interview`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the Secretary of State may specify this for an interview` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 23(2) how the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 23(2) when the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 23(2) where the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "how, when and where" are the matters the grant names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (3) "The Secretary of State may, for the purpose of verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement,
-- require a claimant to (a) provide ... information and evidence specified ... in a manner so specified; (b) confirm
-- compliance in a manner so specified."
DECLARE `s 23(3) what the claimant may be required to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(3)(a) provide information and evidence in the manner specified`
    `s 23(3)(b) confirm compliance in the manner specified`
    `s 23(3) something else`

-- src:258 | (3) The Secretary of State may, for the purpose of verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement, require a claimant to—
-- src:259 | (a) provide to the Secretary of State information and evidence specified by the Secretary of State in a manner so specified;
-- src:260 | (b) confirm compliance in a manner so specified.
@ref s 23(3) (src:258-260)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 23(3) what the claimant may be required to do`
      `the purpose is verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) the Secretary of State may require the claimant to do this` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is verifying the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement`
    THEN
        CONSIDER requirement
        WHEN `s 23(3)(a) provide information and evidence in the manner specified` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 23(3)(b) confirm compliance in the manner specified` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) and (b) are the two things the power names
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "for the purpose of verifying the claimant's compliance"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) "The Secretary of State may require a claimant to report ... any specified changes in their circumstances which are
-- relevant to (a) the imposition of work-related requirements on the claimant; (b) the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement."
-- src:261 | (4) The Secretary of State may require a claimant to report to the Secretary of State any specified changes in their circumstances which are relevant to—
-- src:262 | (a) the imposition of work-related requirements on the claimant;
-- src:263 | (b) the claimant's compliance with a work-related requirement.
@ref s 23(4) (src:261-263)
GIVEN `the change is one the Secretary of State has specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is relevant to the imposition of requirements or to the claimant's compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) the Secretary of State may require the claimant to report the change` MEANS
    IF `the change is one the Secretary of State has specified` AND `the change is relevant to the imposition of requirements or to the claimant's compliance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any specified changes in their circumstances which are relevant to" (a) or (b)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 24 -- Imposition of requirements`

-- (2) "Where the Secretary of State may impose a work-focused interview requirement, or specify a particular action under
-- section 16(1) or 17(1)(b), the Secretary of State must have regard to such matters as may be prescribed."
-- src:269 | (2) Where the Secretary of State may impose a work-focused interview requirement, or specify a particular action under section 16(1) or 17(1)(b), the Secretary of State must have regard to such matters as may be prescribed.
@ref s 24(2) (src:269-269)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State may impose a work-focused interview requirement or specify an action under section 16(1) or 17(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) the Secretary of State must have regard to the matters regulations prescribe` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State may impose a work-focused interview requirement or specify an action under section 16(1) or 17(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for the case where the Secretary of State "may impose" or "specify"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3) "may revoke or change what has been imposed or specified."
-- src:270 | (3) Where the Secretary of State may impose a requirement under this Part, or specify any action to be taken in relation to such a requirement, the Secretary of State may revoke or change what has been imposed or specified.
@ref s 24(3) (src:270-270)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State may impose the requirement or specify the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(3) the Secretary of State may revoke or change what has been imposed or specified` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State may impose the requirement or specify the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for the case where the Secretary of State "may impose a requirement under this Part, or specify any action"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) "Notification of a requirement imposed under this Part (or any change to or revocation of such a requirement) is, if not
-- included in the claimant commitment, to be in such manner as the Secretary of State may determine."
-- src:271 | (4) Notification of a requirement imposed under this Part (or any change to or revocation of such a requirement) is, if not included in the claimant commitment, to be in such manner as the Secretary of State may determine.
@ref s 24(4) (src:271-271)
GIVEN `the requirement is included in the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(4) notification is in the manner the Secretary of State may determine` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is included in the claimant commitment`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the manner is the Secretary of State's to determine only "if not included in the claimant commitment"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5)(a) "a requirement imposed on that claimant under this Part ceases to have effect for a period of 13 weeks": 91 days, both ends counting.
-- src:272 | (5) Regulations must make provision to secure that, in prescribed circumstances, where a claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence—
-- src:273 | (a) a requirement imposed on that claimant under this Part ceases to have effect for a period of 13 weeks, and
-- src:274 | (b) the Secretary of State may not impose any other requirement under this Part on that claimant during that period.
@ref s 24(5) (src:272-274)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 24(5) the period of 13 weeks` MEANS Period WITH
    `first day` IS `the first day of the period`
    `last day` IS `the first day of the period` PLUS 90

-- (5) "Regulations must make provision to secure that, in prescribed circumstances, where a claimant has recently been a
-- victim of domestic violence (a) a requirement ... ceases to have effect for a period of 13 weeks, and (b) the Secretary of
-- State may not impose any other requirement ... during that period." The first function is (a), the second (b).
@ref s 24(5)(a) (src:273-273)
GIVEN `prescribed circumstances apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of 13 weeks` IS A Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(5)(a) the requirement has ceased to have effect on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day within the period`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `s 3(1) both of these are true` `prescribed circumstances apply` `the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in prescribed circumstances, where a claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence"; outside them the paragraph says nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a period of 13 weeks"; a day outside the period is not covered
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the day within the period` MEANS
            day AT LEAST `the period of 13 weeks`'s `first day` AND day AT MOST `the period of 13 weeks`'s `last day`

@ref s 24(5)(b) (src:274-274)
GIVEN `prescribed circumstances apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of 13 weeks` IS A Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(5)(b) the Secretary of State may impose another requirement on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day within the period`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `s 3(1) both of these are true` `prescribed circumstances apply` `the claimant has recently been a victim of domestic violence`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary of State may not impose any other requirement under this Part on that claimant during that period"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for prescribed circumstances in which the claimant has recently been a victim
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during that period"
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the day within the period` MEANS
            day AT LEAST `the period of 13 weeks`'s `first day` AND day AT MOST `the period of 13 weeks`'s `last day`

-- The prohibition in (5)(b) as a regulative rule: the Secretary of State SHANT impose another requirement during the 13 weeks.
-- The first day is time 0, so the 91 days, both ends counting, are times 0 to 90 and WITHIN 90 closes the window on the last
-- day (a trace run on 4 November 2026 showed that WITHIN 91 still treats time 91, the day after the period, as inside it).
@ref s 24(5)(b) (src:274-274)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 13(1) party` `s 13(1) action`
`s 24(5)(b) the Secretary of State shall not impose another requirement during the 13 weeks` MEANS
    PARTY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State`
    SHANT `s 24(5)(b) imposes another requirement`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 13(1) the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "another requirement was imposed within the 13 weeks after a victim of domestic violence's requirement ceased (section 24(5)(b))"

-- (6)(b) "'victim of domestic violence' means a person on or against whom domestic violence is inflicted or threatened (and
-- regulations under subsection (5) may prescribe circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being a
-- victim of domestic violence)". (6)(a) "'domestic violence' has such meaning as may be prescribed", so whether the
-- violence is domestic violence is an input.
-- src:275 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5)—
-- src:276 | (a) “domestic violence” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
@ref s 24(6)(a) (src:275-276)
-- src:277 | (b) “victim of domestic violence“ means a person on or against whom domestic violence is inflicted or threatened (and regulations under subsection (5) may prescribe circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being a victim of domestic violence);
@ref s 24(6)(b) (src:277-277)
GIVEN `domestic violence, as regulations define it, is inflicted or threatened on or against the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the person as being or not being a victim of domestic violence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(6)(b) the person is a victim of domestic violence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations treat the person as being or not being a victim of domestic violence`
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'victim of domestic violence' means a person on or against whom domestic violence is inflicted or threatened"
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "domestic violence" has such meaning as may be prescribed (s 24(6)(a)); where the answer is not supplied it is NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `domestic violence, as regulations define it, is inflicted or threatened on or against the person`

-- (6)(c) "a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a prescribed period has not expired since the violence
-- was inflicted or threatened". A period of p days has expired once p days have passed (fork F-24(6)(c) in NOTES.md).
-- src:278 | (c) a person has recently been a victim of domestic violence if a prescribed period has not expired since the violence was inflicted or threatened.
@ref s 24(6)(c) (src:278-278)
GIVEN `the person is a victim of domestic violence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the days since the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed period in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(6)(c) the person has recently been a victim of domestic violence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed period in days`
    WHEN JUST days THEN
        IF `the days since the violence was inflicted or threatened` LESS THAN days
        THEN `the person is a victim of domestic violence`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a prescribed period has not expired since the violence was inflicted or threatened" (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is prescribed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 25 -- Compliance with requirements`

-- "Regulations may make provision as to circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having (a) complied with or
-- not complied with any requirement imposed under this Part or any aspect of such a requirement, or (b) taken or not taken
-- any particular action specified by the Secretary of State in relation to such a requirement." Where supplied, the
-- regulation replaces the plain fact; NOTHING means no such regulation is supplied.
-- src:280 | Regulations may make provision as to circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having—
-- src:281 | (a) complied with or not complied with any requirement imposed under this Part or any aspect of such a requirement, or
-- src:282 | (b) taken or not taken any particular action specified by the Secretary of State in relation to such a requirement.
@ref s 25 (src:280-282)
GIVEN `the claimant in fact complied or took the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the claimant as having complied or taken the action, or not` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25 the claimant is treated as having complied or taken the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations treat the claimant as having complied or taken the action, or not`
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claimant in fact complied or took the action`

§ `Section 26 -- Higher-level sanctions`

-- (1) "The amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure
-- by a claimant which is sanctionable under this section."
-- src:285 | (1) The amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by a claimant which is sanctionable under this section.
@ref s 26(1) (src:285-285)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the amount of the award is to be reduced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the failure is sanctionable under section 26`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reduction is "in the event of a failure ... sanctionable under this section"; with no such failure this section is silent
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the failure is sanctionable
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2) "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant falling within section 22 (a) fails for no good reason
-- to comply with a requirement ... to undertake a work placement of a prescribed description; (b) fails for no good reason
-- to comply with a requirement ... to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work; (c) fails for no good reason to comply
-- with a work availability requirement by not taking up an offer of paid work; (d) by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily
-- and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay." (5)(a) lets regulations treat ceasing work or losing pay as by
-- misconduct or voluntary or not, and (5)(b) lets loss of pay below a prescribed level be disregarded; the two facts below
-- are asked as regulations treat them.
DECLARE `s 26(2) kind of failure` IS ONE OF
    `s 26(2)(a) failing to undertake a work placement`
    `s 26(2)(b) failing to apply for a particular vacancy`
    `s 26(2)(c) not taking up an offer of paid work`
    `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay`

-- src:296 | (5) For the purposes of subsections (2) to (4) regulations may provide—
-- src:297 | (a) for circumstances in which ceasing to work or losing pay is to be treated as occurring or not occurring by reason of misconduct or voluntarily;
-- src:298 | (b) for loss of pay below a prescribed level to be disregarded.
@ref s 26(5) (src:296-298)
-- src:286 | (2) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant falling within section 22—
-- src:287 | (a) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement imposed by the Secretary of State under a work preparation requirement to undertake a work placement of a prescribed description;
-- src:288 | (b) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement imposed by the Secretary of State under a work search requirement to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work;
-- src:289 | (c) fails for no good reason to comply with a work availability requirement by not taking up an offer of paid work;
-- src:290 | (d) by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay.
@ref s 26(2) (src:286-290)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 26(2) kind of failure`
      `the claimant falls within section 22` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the placement is of a description regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the ceasing or loss of pay was by reason of misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ceasing or loss of pay was voluntary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss of pay is below the prescribed level and regulations disregard it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 26` MEANS
    `s 3(1) both of these are true` `the claimant falls within section 22` `the failure is of the kind`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant falling within section 22 ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
    WHERE
        `no good reason` MEANS NOT `the claimant had a good reason`
        `the failure is of the kind` MEANS
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `s 26(2)(a) failing to undertake a work placement` THEN
                `s 3(1) both of these are true` (JUST `no good reason`) `the placement is of a description regulations prescribe`
            WHEN `s 26(2)(b) failing to apply for a particular vacancy` THEN JUST `no good reason`
            WHEN `s 26(2)(c) not taking up an offer of paid work` THEN JUST `no good reason`
            WHEN `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` THEN
                `s 3(1) both of these are true`
                    (JUST (`the ceasing or loss of pay was by reason of misconduct` OR (`the ceasing or loss of pay was voluntary` AND `no good reason`)))
                    (`s 4(1)(d) the opposite of this` `the loss of pay is below the prescribed level and regulations disregard it`)

-- (3) "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, a
-- claimant falling within section 19 by virtue of subsection (3) of that section ceases paid work or loses pay so as to cease
-- to fall within that section and to fall within section 22 instead."
-- src:291 | (3) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, a claimant falling within section 19 by virtue of subsection (3) of that section ceases paid work or loses pay so as to cease to fall within that section and to fall within section 22 instead.
@ref s 26(3) (src:291-291)
GIVEN `the claimant fell within section 19 by virtue of subsection (3) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `so as to cease to fall within section 19 and to fall within section 22 instead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) the failure is sanctionable under section 26` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, a claimant falling within section 19 by virtue of subsection (3) ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
    `the claimant fell within section 19 by virtue of subsection (3) of that section`
    AND `the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason`
    AND `so as to cease to fall within section 19 and to fall within section 22 instead`

-- (4) "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if, at any time before making the claim by reference to which the
-- award is made, the claimant (a) for no good reason failed to take up an offer of paid work, or (b) by reason of misconduct,
-- or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceased paid work or lost pay, and at the time the award is made the claimant falls within section 22."
-- src:292 | (4) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if, at any time before making the claim by reference to which the award is made, the claimant—
-- src:293 | (a) for no good reason failed to take up an offer of paid work, or
-- src:294 | (b) by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceased paid work or lost pay,
-- src:295 | and at the time the award is made the claimant falls within section 22.
@ref s 26(4) (src:292-295)
GIVEN `before making the claim the claimant for no good reason failed to take up an offer of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before making the claim the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the award is made the claimant falls within section 22` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(4) the earlier failure is sanctionable under section 26` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if, at any time before making the claim ..., the claimant (a) ... or (b) ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
    `s 3(1) both of these are true`
        (JUST (`before making the claim the claimant for no good reason failed to take up an offer of paid work`
               OR `before making the claim the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason`))
        `at the time the award is made the claimant falls within section 22`

-- (6)(b) regulations are to provide for "the period for which such a reduction has effect, not exceeding three years in
-- relation to any failure sanctionable under this section": the period starts on its first day and, counting both ends, may
-- last up to the day before the third anniversary (calendar years, `add years`; leap days are not tested).
-- src:299 | (6) Regulations are to provide for—
-- src:300 | (a) the amount of a reduction under this section;
-- src:301 | (b) the period for which such a reduction has effect, not exceeding three years in relation to any failure sanctionable under this section.
@ref s 26(6) (src:299-301)
GIVEN period IS A Period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(6)(b) the period of the reduction does not exceed three years` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not exceeding three years in relation to any failure sanctionable under this section"
    period's `last day` LESS THAN `add years` (period's `first day`) 3

§ `Section 27 -- Other sanctions`

-- (1) as s 26(1), for failures sanctionable under this section.
-- src:310 | (1) The amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced in accordance with this section in the event of a failure by a claimant which is sanctionable under this section.
@ref s 27(1) (src:310-310)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the amount of the award is to be reduced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the failure is sanctionable under section 27`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reduction is "in the event of a failure ... sanctionable under this section"; with no such failure this section is silent
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the failure is sanctionable
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2) "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant (a) fails for no good reason to comply with a
-- work-related requirement; (b) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement under section 23." (3) "But a failure
-- by a claimant is not sanctionable under this section if it is also a failure sanctionable under section 26."
-- Whether the claimant failed is the fact as s 25 leaves it (the caller passes the result of `s 25 ...`).
-- src:311 | (2) It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant—
-- src:312 | (a) fails for no good reason to comply with a work-related requirement;
-- src:313 | (b) fails for no good reason to comply with a requirement under section 23.
-- src:314 | (3) But a failure by a claimant is not sanctionable under this section if it is also a failure sanctionable under section 26.
@ref s 27(2) (src:311-314)
GIVEN `the claimant failed to comply with a work-related requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is also sanctionable under section 26` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the failure is sanctionable under section 27` MEANS
    IF (`the claimant failed to comply with a work-related requirement` OR `the claimant failed to comply with a requirement under section 23`)
       AND (NOT `the claimant had a good reason`)
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the failure is also sanctionable under section 26`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure by a claimant is not sanctionable under this section if it is also a failure sanctionable under section 26"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not known whether the failure is also sanctionable under section 26
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a failure sanctionable under this section if a claimant (a) fails for no good reason ...; (b) ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
