§ `Section 28 -- Hardship payments`

-- (1) "Regulations may make provision for the making of additional payments by way of universal credit to a claimant
-- ('hardship payments') where (a) the amount of the claimant's award is reduced under section 26 or 27, and (b) the claimant
-- is or will be in hardship." Whether the claimant is in hardship is for regulations (s 28(2)(a)-(b)).
-- src:338 | (1) Regulations may make provision for the making of additional payments by way of universal credit to a claimant (“hardship payments”) where—
-- src:339 | (a) the amount of the claimant's award is reduced under section 26 or 27, and
-- src:340 | (b) the claimant is or will be in hardship.
@ref s 28(1) (src:338-340)
GIVEN `regulations make provision for hardship payments` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the claimant's award is reduced under section 26 or 27` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is or will be in hardship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) a hardship payment may be made to the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations make provision for hardship payments`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the amount of the claimant's award is reduced under section 26 or 27`
        THEN
            CONSIDER `the claimant is or will be in hardship`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is for payments "where ... the claimant is or will be in hardship"
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the claimant is in hardship is for regulations (s 28(2)(a), (b)), not among the sources
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is for payments "where the amount of the claimant's award is reduced under section 26 or 27"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (a supplied regulation says no): "Regulations may make provision for the making of additional payments"; the regulations the caller supplies make no provision
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): hardship payments exist only if regulations provide them; they are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2)(f) "whether hardship payments are recoverable": seam 4 of PLAN.md. Returns the regulations' answer as supplied (it
-- is a MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that NOTHING stays NOTHING).
-- src:347 | (f) whether hardship payments are recoverable.
@ref s 28(2)(f) (src:347-347)
GIVEN `the regulations' answer, if supplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2)(f) the hardship payment is recoverable under section 28` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "whether hardship payments are recoverable" is for regulations, which are not among the sources
    `the regulations' answer, if supplied`

§ `Section 29 -- Delegation and contracting out`

-- (1) "The functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25 may be exercised by, or by the employees of, such
-- person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose (an 'authorised person')."
-- src:350 | (1) The functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25 may be exercised by, or by the employees of, such person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose (an “authorised person”).
@ref s 29(1) (src:350-350)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
      `the Secretary of State has authorised the person for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) this authority may exercise the Secretary of State's functions under sections 13 to 25` MEANS
    CONSIDER authority
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection is about "such person as the Secretary of State may authorise"; the Secretary of State's own power to exercise these functions is given by sections 13 to 25 themselves
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Secretary of State has authorised the person for the purpose`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose"; a person not so authorised is outside the grant
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) "Anything done or omitted to be done by or in relation to an authorised person (or an employee of that person) in, or in
-- connection with, the exercise or purported exercise of the function concerned is to be treated for all purposes as done or
-- omitted to be done by or in relation to the Secretary of State". (5) "Subsection (4) does not apply (a) for the purposes
-- of so much of any contract made between the authorised person and the Secretary of State as relates to the exercise of
-- the function, or (b) for the purposes of any criminal proceedings brought in respect of anything done or omitted to be
-- done by the authorised person (or an employee of that person)."
DECLARE `s 29(4) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 29(5)(a) the contract between the authorised person and the Secretary of State`
    `s 29(5)(b) criminal proceedings against the authorised person or an employee`
    `s 29(4) any other purpose`

-- src:359 | (4) Anything done or omitted to be done by or in relation to an authorised person (or an employee of that person) in, or in connection with, the exercise or purported exercise of the function concerned is to be treated for all purposes as done or omitted to be done by or in relation to the Secretary of State or (as the case may be) an officer of the Secretary of State.
-- src:360 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply—
-- src:361 | (a) for the purposes of so much of any contract made between the authorised person and the Secretary of State as relates to the exercise of the function, or
-- src:362 | (b) for the purposes of any criminal proceedings brought in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by the authorised person (or an employee of that person).
@ref s 29(4) (src:359-362)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 29(4) purpose`
      `it was done or omitted by or in relation to an authorised person, or an employee of that person, in exercising or purporting to exercise the function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(4) the act is treated as done by or in relation to the Secretary of State for this purpose` MEANS
    IF `it was done or omitted by or in relation to an authorised person, or an employee of that person, in exercising or purporting to exercise the function`
    THEN
        CONSIDER purpose
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply (a) for the purposes of so much of any contract ..."
        WHEN `s 29(5)(a) the contract between the authorised person and the Secretary of State` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply ... (b) for the purposes of any criminal proceedings ..."
        WHEN `s 29(5)(b) criminal proceedings against the authorised person or an employee` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `s 29(4) any other purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) is for things done "by or in relation to an authorised person ... in ... the exercise or purported exercise of the function"
    ELSE NOTHING
